OVMX THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE NOTICES AND WRITTEN OFFER
===================================================

OVMX is distributed under the GNU General Public License, version 2 (see the
GNU GPL v2 text below). This distribution image also includes, or statically
links, the third-party components listed here. Their license texts and
copyright notices are reproduced below, as required for lawful redistribution.

Bundled / shipped third-party components in this image and kit:

  * Linux kernel (vmlinuz)  -- GNU GPL v2 (GPL-2.0-only). Built from pinned,
    unmodified upstream kernel.org source; OVMX device drivers are overlaid
    in-tree.
  * vms.ko (the OVMX executive kernel module)  -- GNU GPL v2; OVMX's own code.
  * tinycc / TCC.EXE (the bootstrap C compiler)  -- GNU LGPL v2.1. The shipped
    TCC.EXE binary is unmodified upstream tinycc, statically linked.
  * musl libc  -- MIT license. Statically linked into every OVMX .EXE image.

(OpenSSH and LibreSSL are NOT included in this image; when a future release ships
them, their BSD/ISC and OpenSSL/SSLeay notices will be added here.)


WRITTEN OFFER OF CORRESPONDING SOURCE (GPL v2 section 3 / LGPL v2.1 section 4)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

The complete corresponding source code for every GPL- and LGPL-licensed
component in this distribution -- the Linux kernel, vms.ko, tinycc, and OVMX
itself -- is available, for a period of at least three (3) years from the date
of this distribution, as follows:

  * OVMX (including vms.ko and OVMX's own sources), the exact pinned Linux
    kernel version, and the exact pinned tinycc source, are all published in the
    OVMX source repository, from which this image was built. The tinycc source
    is additionally included in that repository under third-party/tcc/src/.

  * A copy of the complete corresponding source may also be requested in writing
    from the OVMX distributor. (Distributor contact / repository URL: TO BE
    FILLED IN BY THE PUBLISHER AT RELEASE -- this offer is not valid until a
    concrete source location and/or contact address is supplied here.)

For the statically-linked LGPL v2.1 component (tinycc / TCC.EXE), the complete
corresponding source and the OVMX object files or build recipe sufficient to
relink a modified tinycc are available from the same source repository, as
required by LGPL v2.1 section 6.

The full license texts follow.

